From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Retain notices for copied third-party code

The upstream source identifies code copied from Data::Dump and
String::PerlQuote. Retain their attribution and Perl licensing terms.

--- /dev/null
+++ b/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+Data::Dmp includes code identified in its source as copied from Data::Dump.
+The corresponding code and notice were checked against the official
+Data-Dump 1.23 release, SHA-256
+af53b05ef1387b4cab4427e6789179283e4f0da8cf036e8db516ddb344512b65.
+That comparison does not establish which Data::Dump release was copied.
+
+Data::Dump was written by Gisle Aas, based on Data::Dumper by Gurusamy Sarathy.
+Copyright 1998-2010 Gisle Aas.
+Copyright 1996-1998 Gurusamy Sarathy.
+The Data::Dump library may be redistributed and modified under the same
+terms as Perl itself. The accompanying LICENSE contains those Perl terms.
+
+Data::Dmp also identifies code copied from String::PerlQuote, copyright 2016
+perlancar@cpan.org, under the same terms as Perl 5. The exact copied release
+has not been established.
